<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00008944> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00008944> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-28"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Glucagon processing in pancreatic A cell (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-10-19 claude4go: Human model; rodent evidence transferred as ISS (GO_REF:0000024, MGI/RGD with/from). Source papers per edge listed in curator file P2GO-rodent-annotations-for-ISS.md: Pax6 rat PMID:20592023, 22778220, 17901057; Mafb mouse PMID:16443760, 29378833; 7B2/Scg5 mouse PMID:10089884, 22013069; Pcsk2 mouse PMID:11356850, 7730317, 40971442; Cpe mouse PMID:11375130. Abstract-level reading only."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-20 ISS replaced by human experimental evidence where found: SCG5 activity occurs in secretory granule, and that granule part of pancreatic A cell -> IDA PMID:1466150 (Azzoni 1992, human pancreas; immuno-EM localises 7B2 to islet secretory granules, strongest in the peripheral halo of alpha granules; note the authors argue 7B2 is unrelated to intracellular prohormone processing, so this reference supports the localisation only). PCSK2 granule part of pancreatic A cell -> IDA PMID:32291281 (Ramzy 2020, immunofluorescence with validated antibodies: PC2 immunoreactivity present in human alpha cells, absent in beta cells). Both read at abstract level only. PAX6, MAFB and CPE edges remain ISS: no human experimental data found."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-20 PMID:9287128 (Rouille 1997, full text read): Fig 3, adenoviral PC2 + Syrian hamster proglucagon in GH4C1 (rat pituitary) cells yields mature glucagon only with PC2; Fig 4, purified recombinant PC2 + CPE convert synthetic human oxyntomodulin to glucagon (CPE alone: no conversion; no PC2-alone lane). Enzyme species not stated (gifts from Lindberg / Fricker), so used as IC on human PCSK2/CPE facts, not IDA/ISS."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-28 CPE enabled by: mouse ISS replaced by IDA PMID:11462236 (Chen 2001 Hum Mutat: wild-type and R283W human CPE cleave peptide substrates; enzyme kinetics and pH profile). Abstract-level reading only; substrates are not glucagon. Other CPE edges and PCSK2 granule/input/process edges remain ISS (no human data found; PMID:8916141 pending full-text check for human immuno-EM of PC2 in alpha granules)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-28 MAFB: ISS replaced by human evidence. MAFB nucleus part of pancreatic A cell -> IDA PMID:34428183 (Shrestha 2021, IHC of non-diabetic human pancreas, MAFB in GCG+ alpha cells, Fig 1E/4D; nuclear localisation not stated explicitly in text). MAFB part of GO:0045944 and has input GCG -> IMP PMID:32488111 (Russell 2020, MAFB-/- hESC differentiated to alpha-like cells: fewer GCG+ cells, reduced GCG mRNA and glucagon content, ARX/PAX6 unchanged, Fig 6; caveat: confounded by an alpha-cell differentiation defect, and GCG is not among MAFB ChIP-seq targets reported there). PAX6: no human IDA/IMP found for alpha cells or GCG (PMID:27941241 shows PAX6 represses GCG in human beta cells); PAX6 edges remain ISS."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-28: added PMID:25811241 (Ramos-Molina & Lindberg 2015, full text). FAM20C (human) phosphorylates 7B2 at Thr73/Thr111 (IDA, human 7B2 in HEK cells, Fig 6A); phosphomimetic T111E (rat 7B2) reduces activation of human proPC2 in human SK-N-MC cells (IMP, Fig 5A) -> FAM20C directly negatively regulates SCG5. Human 7B2 required for human PC2 activity in SK-N-MC (Fig 5B/6B) -> IDA replaces mouse ISS on SCG5 enabled_by and SCG5 -> PCSK2. Not studied in alpha cells or islets: FAM20C Golgi part_of A cell is IC (curator decision). Ala100-lacking 7B2 splice variant activates proPC2 less efficiently (not modelled as an isoform)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Caveats: (1) FOXA2 not modelled: rat G2 Foxa site not conserved in human (PMID:15828872). (2) CPE part_of pancreatic A cell is IC: no A cell-specific CPE localization paper found. (3) CPE has_input is GCG (P01275) standing for the PC2 product glucagon-Lys-Arg; no UniProt chain for it. (4) Some ISS sources (e.g. mouse Scg5 GO:0016504, secretory granule) are not yet in GOA; pending P2GO entry by curator."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

